_the_Bodhi_Tree_Bharhut_relief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Adoration_of_the_Diamond_Throne_and_the_Bodhi_Tree_Bharhut_relief.jpg/500px-Adoration_of_the_Diamond_Throne_and_the_Bodhi_Tree_Bharhut_relief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ashoka's Mahabodhi Temple and Diamond throne in Bodh Gaya, built circa 250 BCE. The inscription between the chaitya arches reads: \"Bhagavato Sakamunino/ bodho\", meaning \"the building round the Bodhi tree of the Holy Sakamuni\".[28] Bharhut frieze (circa 100 BCE).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdoration_of_the_Diamond_Throne_and_the_Bodhi_Tree_Bharhut_relief.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bodhi_tree_in_Theosophical_Society.jpg/500px-Bodhi_tree_in_Theosophical_Society.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bodhi_tree_in_Theosophical_Society.jpg/500px-Bodhi_tree_in_Theosophical_Society.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sapling of the Maha bodhi tree planted in the year 1950 at the Theosophical Society Adyar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABodhi_tree_in_Theosophical_Society.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}